#!/usr/bin/python3
# sg-apt-sources -- keep third-party apt sources from blocking every update.
#
# apt refuses to read any of its sources when two entries for one repository
# disagree on an option: "E: Conflicting values set for option Signed-By
# regarding source https://packages.mozilla.org/apt/ mozilla: A != B" and then
# "E: The list of sources could not be read." -- no update from anywhere, not
# even Debian's security updates. It happens when a repository is added twice:
# SG Store's Firefox puts packages.mozilla.org in mozilla.list with the key in
# /usr/share/keyrings, and Mozilla's own instructions append the same
# repository with the key in /etc/apt/keyrings (a VM of David's, 2026-10-06).
#
#   sg-apt-sources heal            make the sources readable again; prints what
#                                  it changed (and logs it), exits 0 unless it
#                                  could not
#   sg-apt-sources adopt FILE      SG Store: put the maker's source FILE in place
#                                  unless the same repository is configured
#                                  already (any file, one-line or deb822), then
#                                  heal; prints "reuse PATH" or "added PATH"
#   sg-apt-sources problems        read `apt-get update` output on stdin; print
#                                  one line per repository it could not use:
#                                  "HOST<TAB>reason" (Settings > Updates shows
#                                  them; the other repositories still update)
#
# heal: entries for one repository and suite that name different keyrings get
# one keyring -- a system one (Debian's, ours) if involved, else the first in
# apt's order whose file exists -- and an entry that then repeats another is
# turned off. Any other "Conflicting values"/"Malformed entry" error apt still
# reports turns off the later entry (a one-line entry is commented out, a
# deb822 stanza gets "Enabled: no", an unreadable file is renamed
# NAME.sg-disabled). Debian's and Stained Glass OS's own sources are never
# turned off. Each changed file is first copied to /var/backups/sg-apt-sources.
#
# SG_APT_ROOT (default /) is the root the files are under, for the gate
# (SG_APT_ETC, if set, is its etc/apt); apt itself is run with whatever
# APT_CONFIG says.
#
